  - (4) Piers, docks, wharves, breakwaters and uses projecting into water bodies;

  - (5) The installation of essential services, other than roadside distribution lines, is not allowed in a Resource Protection District, except to provide services to a permitted use within said district, or except where the applicant demonstrates that no reasonable alternative exists. Where allowed, such structures and facilities shall be located so as to minimize any adverse impacts on surrounding uses and resources, including visual impacts;

